WEBVTT

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.660
Shimamura...

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.040
Shimamu...

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.660
Yummy!

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.450
Is it that weird to walk around town
on Christmas with Shimamura?

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.950
No matter how many times I try to visualize it,
weird things keep happening.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.250
Lately, it's been so cold
on the second floor of the gym,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.000
so we haven't been going up there.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.580
I want to see her.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.370
I want to spend special time alone with her.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.040
"Shimamura"

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.040
"Hey, on Christmas..."
And to make that happen, I figured
the best bet would be Christmas, but...

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.200
And to make that happen, I figured
the best bet would be Christmas, but...

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.120
"Shimamura"

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.120
"Hey, on Christmas..."
The problem would be to actually
ask her to hang out on Christmas.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.750
The problem would be to actually
ask her to hang out on Christmas.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.870
"Shimamura"

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.580
I don't know if I just wrote it extra hard,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.830
"Shimamura"

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.830
but even after I erased it,
you could still see her name.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.330
It's sort of like when I close my eyes
to sleep, and even when tomorrow comes,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.700
I can't forget about Shimamura

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.000
"Christmas"

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.000
from the day before.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.540
Whenever Shimamura asks me to do anything,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.160
I wonder how much I'd end up complying.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.660
Hold my bag.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.500
Wait, wrong mood.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.040
Carry me.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.910
Would I try? I probably would.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.580
Let's take a nap together.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.620
Wh-What's with me?!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.120
I've been so wrapped up with trying to ask
Shimamura to hang out on Christmas...

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.250
I feel like I almost went off the edge,

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:33.750
climbed up a tree,
and can't come back down now.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.370
Hey, there, Shimako.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.660
Did you need something?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.660
Nope. What? Do I need a reason
to talk to my buddy?

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.120
Usually, yeah.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.120
Pretty much.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.830
Yo. Studying hard, Adacchi?

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.830
Uh... I guess.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.330
Wait, you are? Wow, how studious of you.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.500
Huh?! I, uh...

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.200
Alrighty! Let's go to Nagafuji's place today!

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.410
I can't shake the feeling that you end up
near our <i>kotatsu </i>like every day.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.540
Nah, you're just imagining it.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.200
Did you need something?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.870
No, wait. My bad.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.290
What's wrong? Wait, how is that any different?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.120
What should I say?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.040
Wait, you're asking me?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.830
I guess I'll just keep thinking about this.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.290
So, what were you trying to ask me, Adachi?

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.500
Huh? I, uh...

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.620
"Hey, on Christmas..."

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.950
Let's...

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:00.330
Let's study together... or something.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.500
Study? Then we should invite
Hino and Nagafuji, too.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.330
No, wait, um...

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.540
Well, they're smarter than us.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:13.910
Which means they'd get nothing
out of studying with us...

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:18.950
Oh, I see. You think that
our grades are about the same,

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.950
and we're about the same level of stupid.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.290
Huh? I, uh...

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:30.830
Jeez, I'm kidding. Sure.
Why don't we study together?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.450
Where should we study? The library?

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.540
Or maybe a family restaurant.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.250
Or maybe...

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:40.500
At home! At your house!

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.660
Would that be okay?

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.200
What? It's really dusty, though.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.120
Wha--?

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.660
What about your room, Adachi?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.410
My room?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.620
I don't know about my place...

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.580
Actually, that would be
a bit awkward for me, too.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.410
Then, sure. Let's go to my place.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.700
Even if it's dusty.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.330
What's up?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.200
C-Coming!

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.660
I'm home!

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.330
Welcome back.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.830
Whoa, a friend. Whoa, in our house.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.160
Um... Whoa?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.040
Adachi, was it? Welcome.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.000
Thanks...

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.750
Come on. Let's go to my room.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.500
Thanks for letting me come over.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.540
Wait, isn't your room this way?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.910
Adachi!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.410
Come on. My study room is upstairs.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.830
"Parakeety"   "Croquette"   "Li'l Cutlet"

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.250
Yeah, none of these are doing it for me.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.330
Why don't you say how you really feel?

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.580
Okay, how about this one?

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:52.870
This is definitely the next mascot
for the Nagafuji Butcher Shop!

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.040
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.040
This is definitely the next mascot
for the Nagafuji Butcher Shop!

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.660
Li'l Croquette, eh?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.200
Yeah, I guess that'll work.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:05.750
Don't you mean, "That's the one"?
You even gave her a name.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.620
Well, I'll give you a treat.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:14.160
Sweet! Wait, is it another
kiss on the forehead?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.620
You don't want it?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.200
Er, yeah... I guess I'll take it.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.080
You two are so close.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.870
Hey, Auntie...

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.250
You'll have mandarins, won't you?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.160
Close... Are we close?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.080
Not any more than normal.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:57.290
I mean, we get along like normal friends.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.160
Jeez, it's cold.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.950
See? I told you it was dusty.
This is my study room.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:13.250
Until things warm up, I call for a break.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.910
Do you usually listen to music
while you study, Adachi?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.120
Y-Yeah, pretty often.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.540
I see...

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.750
Um... I...

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.870
On Ch... Chri...

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.950
So, what kind of kid were you, Shimamura?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.290
Um... Pretty normal?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:40.000
I feel like I was always the kid
serving lunch to the other kids.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:46.620
Oh, and I think my hair was shorter,
and not dyed.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:51.910
Shimamura with short hair... With black hair...

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:53.700
I'd love to see that.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.540
What were you like, Adachi?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:02.450
Huh?! I, uh... haven't really changed.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:08.080
Huh... I picture you holding
the preschool teacher's hand.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:12.580
I wasn't like that at all.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.450
Then what were you like?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.910
I was, uh... I'm particular
about whose hand I hold...

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:26.200
What the heck am I saying?!
Now I sound like I'm asking her out!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:32.160
Huh... I wonder why you hold mine, then.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.330
So, uh, earlier...

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:57.200
Shimamura had asked why it was her...

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.200
Why? It's rather simple, really.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.700
It's because you're Shimamura.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:09.620
If I were to just come out and say that,

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:13.500
I'd basically be saying,
"I love you, Shimamura."

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.910
So...

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:27.950
No, no, get a hold of yourself!

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.080
If she woke up and you were kissing her,

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.290
it'd really be game over!

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:37.870
And it's not like I
absolutely need to kiss her...

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:42.120
I mean, I wouldn't be opposed
if Shimamura asked for one...

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.790
But she didn't...

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.120
Er, I was just--

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.290
Huh? Wha--?!

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.830
There we go...

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.080
This is much softer and pleasant.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:09.790
Huh? A-Ah, I shee...

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.950
A-Are you a little sleepyhead?

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.830
I sure am...

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.950
Here. It's cold.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.500
Th-Thanks...

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.790
Hey, Shimamura...

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.370
Hm?

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.450
So, Shimamura... Um...

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.700
Chri...

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.370
What do you usually do on Christmas?!

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.580
We get fried chicken for dinner...

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.080
Oh, and cake.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:45.910
Th-That's not what I meant...

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:49.790
My little sister still believes
in Santa Claus, too.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:52.330
Santa...

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:55.700
How long did you believe in Santa?

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.870
Hm? I didn't, really.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.330
There's no way a nice old man
like that actually exists.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.000
What about you, Adachi?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.950
I thought... he was at my preschool.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.330
Wait, what?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:14.250
I think it's because the only people to ever
talk about Santa were at my preschool...

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.580
I guess we both sorta sucked at childhood.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.040
Yeah...

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:23.950
But you know... I think we were dumber
and more uninhibited when we were kids.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:27.580
It's amazing we survived at all.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:32.750
Must be nice. Probably never experienced
stiff shoulders back then.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.330
Never mind.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.450
Right now, I just want to stay
like this with Shimamura.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:46.870
Like I'm protecting my precious
child with my wings...

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.500
Just like this.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.290
Adachi's been acting weird lately.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.500
I feel her staring at me a lot more.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.660
That's the first weird thing.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:05.790
The second thing is when we're talking,
she seems to always be holding back.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.000
I'm not sure how her lips haven't cramped yet.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:12.200
And the third thing...

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.870
Sh-Shimamura!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.410
Um... I, uh...

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.700
I-I'm going to the bathroom.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:27.500
She scored higher on
our English test than I did.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:30.870
Though the third thing has
nothing to do with anything.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.160
But...

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.370
--Ow...
--Huh? Shimamura?!

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.040
S-Sorry! Actually, what are you doing?

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:53.200
I was just having a little bit of fun.
More importantly...

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.580
U-Um, Shimamura?

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.580
Okay, take a deep breath!

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:05.790
Go.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:13.410
Yo, Adacchi...

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.870
I'd prefer if you didn't call me that.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:23.290
Fear not. I probably won't use
that nickname again. So...

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.500
I've just been wondering what's up.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.910
What's up?

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.950
You're always staring at me.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.910
You think so?

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:32.000
Yes.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.750
Is there something you want to tell me?

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.410
Sorta...

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.790
Then tell me.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:47.200
So, this winter... I mean, next week, I mean...

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.200
In about ten days...

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.120
Ten days?

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:53.120
I, uh, um...

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.250
You've got this, me!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.870
I'll tell you after I think on it some more.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.040
I see.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:08.950
There was a girl I was really close
with in kindergarten.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:15.370
She would always hide behind me and
to put it simply, she was like Adachi.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:19.750
This is when I was still unguarded,
still had interest in everything,

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.500
and dove headfirst into them.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:27.750
She really loved sparkly things
like marbles and wind chimes.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:30.910
It was only when she found sparkly things

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:35.000
that she'd leave my side and run towards them.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:46.540
Let's take a look at the image
trending on social media today.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.370
--You got your lunch bag?
--Oh? They both have their hands raised.

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:50.410
--Yup. Bye!
--Oh? They both have their hands raised.

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:53.200
You should get to school, too, Sis.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:55.040
Shush your mouth.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:59.910
High schoolers only need to get to
school before the sun goes up fully.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:04.160
Who taught you that dumb rule? Hurry and eat.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.950
Sis! Sis!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:11.950
Your friend is here! That girl!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:15.120
Huh? Uh... Friend?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.410
The one that came over the other day.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.830
Huh? What?!

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.370
Bye.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.790
How ya doin', Adachi?

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.120
H-Heyo... Mornin'.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.910
Why are you trying to sound like a jock?
So, what's up?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:03.040
It's a bit early, isn't it?
Actually, when did you get here?

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:09.080
I had to stop by somewhere...
This is pretty normal, and I just got here.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.290
Hm.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.410
You're freezing.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:23.540
It's cold, so let's talk inside.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.410
Th-Thank you.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:32.700
Help her eat, would you? She's so slow,
I just don't know what to do with her.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.620
You don't need to say any of that.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:39.410
Um... I ate at home, so...

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.790
What did you eat?

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:43.330
Um... One bread.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:47.080
You need to eat more!
Doesn't your mom tell you that?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.620
Honestly!

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:54.000
As a mom, you feel better when your
daughter is a bit pudgy and doesn't

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.790
wither away worrying about her waistline.

00:17:56.790 --> 00:18:01.450
She doesn't. We don't really talk much.
She's rarely home.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:02.830
Oh, I see.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.450
Fanks for the grub.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.370
Okay, let's go talk in my room.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:16.500
Yeesh, it's cold.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:20.950
I just turned the heater on,
so make yourself at home.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.250
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.870
I asked you that yesterday, too.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:30.370
Y-Yeah, I, uh...

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:35.200
I, um...

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:38.870
Shimamura!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.330
Huh?! Y-Yes?

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:44.870
Do you want to go out somewhere... or something?

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:48.830
Hm? Sure... Wait, that's it?

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.870
Sure, but after school, right?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.370
You don't mean like right now
and skip school, do you?

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:56.910
Oh, not today... you see.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:59.160
Oh, I see. Sure.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.290
I-I...

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.250
I was wondering about the 25th of this month!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.200
The 25th? The 25th...

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:17.660
December 25th... Oh, that 25th.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.620
Yeah.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.370
You mean Christmas, right?

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.200
Yeah...

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.500
Wh--?

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:30.290
I almost asked her why, but I stopped myself.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.660
Why Christmas? Why with me?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:38.120
If I asked her why, I felt like
the backbone of our relationship

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.620
would get bent out of shape.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:46.620
It would take a bunch of time
and effort to fix it later,

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.790
and I wondered if I'd even bother with it,

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.200
though the answer was sadly pretty clear.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:56.040
So...

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.450
Where did you want to go?

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:03.910
I haven't really thought it out at all.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.120
Well, what did you want to do?

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:09.080
I haven't really thought it out at all.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.950
But what do you say?

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:13.580
I'd like to think that

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:18.910
Adachi never got to have
the full Christmas experience

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:22.410
and that's why she asked me.

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:25.250
I mean, just looking at how she's
acting and how red her face is...

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.750
It's basically like...

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.250
She's asking me out.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.580
Oh, it's not a big deal or anything.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.330
I just... I think I just
maybe wanted to hang out

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:40.580
with someone on a fun day like Christmas.

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.370
Not maybe. I do want to.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.290
Oh...

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:49.540
She just wanted to hang out with someone.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:55.370
And she doesn't have any other friends,
so that's why she asked me.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:59.950
It didn't have to be me specifically. I see.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.700
Well, in that case...

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.330
I need to be home by dinner,
but if you're okay with that...

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:08.410
R-Really?!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:11.950
If you're going to decide where
we're going to go and everything.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:25.250
Adachi?

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.830
Wittle puppy Adachi.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.450
Er, never mind.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.330
Huh?

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.870
W-We should get to school.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:43.250
Huh? Right... Then let's go together...

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:49.250
Let us hurry. Yes. Oh, I'm going to be so busy!

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.330
A-Adachi?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.950
Oh, so busy...

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.830
W-Wait.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.700
Wait for li'l ol' me!

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:05.450
Why did I go all old timey?

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:08.040
Let me catch a ride!

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:14.700
Well, whatever.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:20.660
And so, I guess I'm hanging out
with Adachi this Christmas.

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:25.660
"Episode 5: 'Adachi's Question'"

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:25.660
I mean, it's not like Santa's coming by,
even if I waited at home.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:28.040
"Episode 5: 'Adachi's Question'"

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.040
"Next Time: 'White Album'"

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.200
"Next Time: 'White Album'"

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.200
Adashimapedia: <i>Kotatsu</i>.

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:03.330
"Next Time: 'White Album'"

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:03.330
<i>Kotatsu </i>tables just ruin everyone.

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:04.580
"Next Time: 'White Album'"

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:04.580
Right?

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:05.700
Get me some tea.

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:07.450
Nope. I'm not leaving this warmth.

00:24:07.450 --> 00:24:08.290
Do the preview.

00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:10.250
Nope, too cozy.

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:11.200
Well, whatever.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:13.040
Good, good.
